From: erosqcfw <erosqcfw@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] player: cap decoded read-ahead while paused

A paused song keeps the decoder filling the music pipe until the whole
audio_buffer_size is full of decoded PCM, and that memory stays pinned
for as long as playback is paused.  On EROS Q the state restored at
boot is "paused", so 1 MiB of anonymous memory (of a 26 MB system) was
held at idle.  While paused, stop the decoder at ~1 s of audio
(buffer_before_play, min 16 chunks); unpausing lifts the cap and wakes
the decoder.

---
--- a/src/decoder/Control.hxx	2026-10-03 21:48:57.488221871 +0000
+++ b/src/decoder/Control.hxx	2026-10-03 21:48:57.532800332 +0000
@@ -98,6 +98,16 @@
 	bool seekable;
 
 	/**
+	 * erosq: while the player is paused, the decoder stops
+	 * filling the pipe once it holds this many chunks (0 = no
+	 * limit).  Without it a paused song (e.g. the state restored
+	 * at boot) pins the whole audio_buffer_size of decoded PCM in
+	 * RAM for as long as it stays paused.  Protected by #mutex;
+	 * the player signals #cond when it lowers the limit.
+	 */
+	unsigned pause_chunk_limit = 0;
+
+	/**
 	 * @see #DecoderBridge::initial_seek_essential
 	 */
 	bool initial_seek_essential;
--- a/src/decoder/Bridge.cxx	2026-10-03 21:48:57.496210377 +0000
+++ b/src/decoder/Bridge.cxx	2026-10-03 21:48:57.532895031 +0000
@@ -108,6 +108,17 @@
 		return current_chunk.get();
 
 	do {
+		{
+			/* erosq: paused - don't decode more than
+			   pause_chunk_limit chunks ahead */
+			std::unique_lock lock{dc.mutex};
+			if (dc.pause_chunk_limit > 0 && dc.pipe != nullptr &&
+			    dc.pipe->GetSize() >= dc.pause_chunk_limit) {
+				cmd = NeedChunks(dc, lock);
+				continue;
+			}
+		}
+
 		current_chunk = dc.buffer->Allocate();
 		if (current_chunk != nullptr) {
 			current_chunk->replay_gain_serial = replay_gain_serial;
--- a/src/player/Thread.cxx	2026-10-03 21:48:57.507434810 +0000
+++ b/src/player/Thread.cxx	2026-10-03 21:49:07.010639242 +0000
@@ -1114,6 +1114,7 @@
 
 	std::unique_lock lock{pc.mutex};
 
+	dc.pause_chunk_limit = 0;
 	StartDecoder(lock, pipe, true);
 	ActivateDecoder();
 
@@ -1122,6 +1123,20 @@
 	pc.CommandFinished();
 
 	while (ProcessCommand(lock)) {
+		{
+			/* erosq: cap the decoded read-ahead while
+			   paused (~1 s of audio); lift it and wake the
+			   decoder as soon as playback resumes */
+			const unsigned limit = paused && !decoder_starting
+				? (buffer_before_play > 16U ? buffer_before_play : 16U)
+				: 0U;
+			if (dc.pause_chunk_limit != limit) {
+				dc.pause_chunk_limit = limit;
+				if (limit == 0)
+					dc.Signal();
+			}
+		}
+
 		if (decoder_starting) {
 			/* wait until the decoder is initialized completely */
 
